WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.656 --> 00:00:15.557
judging starts in an hour and a half?"

2
00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:16.618
Nathan cried.

3
00:00:16.638 --> 00:00:18.099
"Oh no!

4
00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:20.781
What if we don't find my painting in time?"

5
00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.222
"Don't worry.

6
00:00:22.602 --> 00:00:25.644
The Lemonade Detectives are on the case," Maggie assured him.

7
00:00:25.664 --> 00:00:27.345
"Come on, guys.

8
00:00:27.385 --> 00:00:28.206
Let's get started!"

9
00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:29.847
Henry nodded.

10
00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:33.510
"First we should look for Patrick near his painting.

11
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.351
Then we can look for Mr.

12
00:00:35.371 --> 00:00:40.494
Collins." "Hannah is probably still at her family's booth," Cole added.

13
00:00:40.514 --> 00:00:43.055
"And what about that weird woman?

14
00:00:43.716 --> 00:00:44.876
We don't know where to find her."

15
00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:49.099
"Maybe she'll go back to the stand for her lemonade," Maggie said.

16
00:00:49.119 --> 00:00:51.941
"She already paid for it, remember?"

17
00:00:52.861 --> 00:00:53.582
Henry nodded.

18
00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:56.303
"Why don't you go back to the lemonade stand?"

19
00:00:56.563 --> 00:00:57.404
he told Maggie.

20
00:00:58.516 --> 00:01:02.858
"You can keep selling lemonade while you watch for all our suspects."

21
00:01:02.878 --> 00:01:05.819
"Especially the sunglasses woman," Cole said.

22
00:01:05.839 --> 00:01:07.440
"Good idea."

23
00:01:09.881 --> 00:01:10.761
Maggie hurried off.

24
00:01:10.781 --> 00:01:15.283
"I know where Patrick's painting is hanging," Nathan told Henry and Cole.

25
00:01:15.303 --> 00:01:16.964
"Come on, I'll show you."

26
00:01:20.765 --> 00:01:23.426
Nathan led the way to another section of the art show.

27
00:01:24.386 --> 00:01:27.868
Patrick's painting was an oil painting of a pretty pond at sunset.

28
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:32.405
"Wow, he really is good," Cole said, studying the painting.

29
00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:35.526
"Do you think this painting will end up in the museum?"

30
00:01:36.566 --> 00:01:38.227
"Never mind that," Henry said.

31
00:01:38.247 --> 00:01:40.587
"I don't see Patrick around here.

32
00:01:41.288 --> 00:01:42.208
Let's look for Hannah."

33
00:01:46.669 --> 00:01:49.650
At the crafts show, Hannah was still at the basket-weaving booth.

34
00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.451
She smiled when she saw the boys coming.

35
00:01:52.471 --> 00:01:55.132
"Hi, lemonade gang," she said.

36
00:01:55.152 --> 00:01:56.392
"Where's Maggie?"

37
00:01:57.312 --> 00:01:58.973
"Selling lemonade," Henry said.

38
00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:01.715
"What have you been doing since we saw you last?"

39
00:02:02.975 --> 00:02:04.256
Hannah looked confused.

40
00:02:04.276 --> 00:02:06.977
"The same thing I've been doing all day."

41
00:02:07.758 --> 00:02:09.479
She held up the basket she was weaving.

42
00:02:09.499 --> 00:02:14.101
"Making baskets, selling baskets, and talking about baskets."

43
00:02:15.202 --> 00:02:17.343
"Did you leave this booth to go anywhere?"

44
00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:18.284
Cole asked.

45
00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.265
"Like over to the art show, for instance?"

46
00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:22.746
Nathan added hopefully.

47
00:02:22.766 --> 00:02:25.528
"I went to the bathroom once."

48
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.160
Hannah frowned.

49
00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.701
"Why are you guys so interested in what I've been doing?"

50
00:02:30.402 --> 00:02:31.542
Suddenly she gasped.

51
00:02:31.562 --> 00:02:35.304
"Wait! Are you investigating a mystery?

52
00:02:36.144 --> 00:02:37.165
Am I a suspect?"

53
00:02:38.225 --> 00:02:39.045
Henry sighed.

54
00:02:39.606 --> 00:02:43.687
That was the only problem with The Lemonade Detectives' success in solving mysteries.

55
00:02:44.928 --> 00:02:47.149
Everyone in town had heard about them by now.

56
00:02:47.789 --> 00:02:49.390
It made it hard to interview people.

57
00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:54.312
"Actually, we are investigating a mystery," he admitted.

58
00:02:55.212 --> 00:02:56.713
"Nathan's painting disappeared."

59
00:02:58.034 --> 00:03:01.016
"Oh." Hannah stared at Nathan with a slight frown.

60
00:03:01.036 --> 00:03:02.938
"You entered the art show?"

61
00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:05.479
"Yes," Nathan said.

62
00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:09.382
"And we heard the judges love his painting," Cole added.

63
00:03:09.402 --> 00:03:12.404
"He might end up winning a spot in the museum.

64
00:03:13.305 --> 00:03:14.786
It's a huge honor, you know!"

65
00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.008
Hannah was still frowning.

66
00:03:17.028 --> 00:03:21.651
"Excuse me," she said, tossing her half-woven basket aside.

67
00:03:21.671 --> 00:03:23.032
"I have to go."

68
00:03:24.584 --> 00:03:26.045
"Wait!" Henry exclaimed.

69
00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:27.927
But it was too late.

70
00:03:28.527 --> 00:03:31.450
Hannah rushed off and disappeared around the corner of the next booth.

71
00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:35.193
"That was weird," Cole said, staring after her.

72
00:03:35.213 --> 00:03:38.675
"Do you think she ran off because she feels guilty?"

73
00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:41.317
"Maybe," Henry said.

74
00:03:41.337 --> 00:03:46.782
"Or maybe she was insulted that we were accusing her of stealing Nathan's painting."

75
00:03:47.843 --> 00:03:48.843
Nathan bit his lip.

76
00:03:49.544 --> 00:03:50.425
"What do we do now?

77
00:03:51.846 --> 00:03:54.248
The judging starts in an hour and ten minutes."

78
00:03:55.428 --> 00:03:58.230
"Let's look for our other suspects," Henry said.

79
00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:02.032
"We can question Hannah again later if necessary."

80
00:04:06.695 --> 00:04:08.176
They hurried back to the art show.

81
00:04:09.116 --> 00:04:11.497
But there was still no sign of Patrick or Mr.

82
00:04:11.537 --> 00:04:16.580
Collins. The park was more crowded than ever as people arrived for the art judging.

83
00:04:17.581 --> 00:04:21.984
Every year people in town loved to join the march over to the museum to display the winning

84
00:04:22.084 --> 00:04:24.360
artwork. "Now what?"

85
00:04:24.621 --> 00:04:25.241
Cole said.

86
00:04:26.281 --> 00:04:27.322
Henry looked at Nathan.

87
00:04:27.342 --> 00:04:30.423
"Why don't you go see if anyone returned your painting?"

88
00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:31.183
he said.

89
00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:33.824
"Cole and I will check in with Maggie."

90
00:04:33.844 --> 00:04:38.807
"Okay." Nathan didn't look very hopeful as he hurried off.

91
00:04:40.948 --> 00:04:45.129
Maggie was pouring lemonade for a middle-aged couple when Henry and Cole arrived.

92
00:04:45.149 --> 00:04:47.010
"Any news?"

93
00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.011
she asked as soon as the couple left.

94
00:04:50.191 --> 00:04:51.112
Henry shook his head.

95
00:04:51.872 --> 00:04:54.033
"We still haven't found Patrick or Mr.

96
00:04:54.073 --> 00:04:58.995
Collins. We did find Hannah, but we only talked to her for a minute."

97
00:04:59.995 --> 00:05:02.096
He quickly described the encounter with Hannah.

98
00:05:02.116 --> 00:05:04.817
"Have you seen any of our suspects?"

99
00:05:05.158 --> 00:05:06.158
Cole asked Maggie.

100
00:05:06.178 --> 00:05:09.159
"Nope." Maggie patted the cashbox.

101
00:05:09.179 --> 00:05:11.560
"I've sold a lot of lemonade.

102
00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.441
But I haven't seen anything suspicious at all."

103
00:05:14.461 --> 00:05:18.703
"The woman with the sunglasses didn't come back for her lemonade?"

104
00:05:18.943 --> 00:05:19.623
Henry asked.

105
00:05:19.643 --> 00:05:21.877
"Nope," Maggie said again.

106
00:05:22.898 --> 00:05:25.440
Just then Nora hurried over to the lemonade stand.

107
00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:27.942
"It's not right!"

108
00:05:28.322 --> 00:05:29.363
she announced loudly.

109
00:05:29.383 --> 00:05:31.645
"About the painting of Patches, I mean."

110
00:05:32.726 --> 00:05:35.388
Henry was too distracted to pay much attention to Nora.

111
00:05:35.408 --> 00:05:37.730
"We know," he told her.

112
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.252
"We're trying to find Nathan's painting.

113
00:05:40.872 --> 00:05:41.433
Don't worry."

114
00:05:41.453 --> 00:05:45.336
"No!" Nora's voice was louder than ever.

115
00:05:45.356 --> 00:05:47.598
"It's not right!

116
00:05:48.299 --> 00:05:49.740
Patches is my kitty.

117
00:05:50.588 --> 00:05:52.070
She shouldn't be in a museum.

118
00:05:52.971 --> 00:05:54.933
She's mine—all mine!

119
00:05:55.414 --> 00:05:57.476
And the picture of her is mine too!"

120
00:05:58.557 --> 00:06:00.440
Spinning around, Nora raced away.
